Bazel separates NVIDIA wheels into different site-packages roots, so their
sibling-relative RPATHs cannot locate one another. Backport the explicit
nvJitLink / cuSPARSE / cuSOLVER preload ordering from Torch 2.8's loader.
This applies only to the pinned Linux x86_64 Python 3.12 Torch wheel.

--- a/site-packages/torch/__init__.py
+++ b/site-packages/torch/__init__.py
@@ -188,8 +188,9 @@
             'cuda_cupti': 'libcupti.so.*[0-9]',
             'cufft': 'libcufft.so.*[0-9]',
             'curand': 'libcurand.so.*[0-9]',
-            'cusolver': 'libcusolver.so.*[0-9]',
+            'nvjitlink': 'libnvJitLink.so.*[0-9]',
             'cusparse': 'libcusparse.so.*[0-9]',
+            'cusolver': 'libcusolver.so.*[0-9]',
             'nccl': 'libnccl.so.*[0-9]',
             'nvtx': 'libnvToolsExt.so.*[0-9]',
         }
